    "result_text": "The full suite (the `AcceptanceTest`, the only test class) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`util/E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 Added a public `toDisplay(String e164)` method (plus a small `groupInThrees` helper) that splits the recognised country calling code from the national digits and renders the country code, a space, then the national digits grouped in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It reuses the existing `longestMatchingCountryCode` logic, falls back to grouping all digits when the code is unknown, and returns the input unchanged for null/malformed values.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived `getTelephoneDisplay()` that delegates to `E164Telephone.toDisplay(telephone)`, following the same pattern as the other computed getters (`getCheckDigit`, `getAgeBand`, etc.).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a matching setter.\n\nBecause MapStruct maps by property name, `getTelephoneDisplay()` \u2192 `setTelephoneDisplay()` wires up automatically, so no change to `OwnerMapper` was needed. The acceptance test's exact assertion (`telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) passes.",
