        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change places each piece of logic in its natural unit and reuses what already exists:\n\n- **Formatting lives in `E164Telephone`**, the class that already owns E.164 knowledge (normalization, country-code table, length rules). `toDisplay` is the read-side complement to `toE164`, and it reuses the existing private `longestMatchingCountryCode` helper rather than duplicating country-code matching \u2014 exactly the right seam. The `NATIONAL_LENGTH`/country-code logic stays in one place.\n- **`groupInThrees`** is a small, focused private helper with a clear doc comment, kept private since it's an implementation detail of display formatting. Reasonable to inline-or-extract, and extracting reads cleanly here.\n- **`Owner.getTelephoneDisplay()`** is a thin derived getter that delegates to the util, matching the established pattern in this class for computed read-only fields (`getAgeBand`, `getMembershipLevel`, `getCheckDigit`, `getIdentityKey`). It correctly keeps `telephone` as the raw stored E.164 and adds display as a separate derived view, per the spec. No formatting logic leaks into the entity.\n- **The OpenAPI `telephoneDisplay`** entry mirrors the shape of the neighbouring derived `readOnly` fields (title/description/example/`readOnly: true`) and its description correctly notes `telephone` stays E.164.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this natural: no catch-all growth, no duplicated country-code handling, and the model/util/contract split follows the conventions already present."
      }
    ]
  }
}